tion"},{"title":"Legacy modernization strategy: a step-by-step plan","slug":"legacy-modernization-strategy","category":"Guide","excerpt":"A legacy modernization strategy is the staged plan for upgrading old systems without breaking the business. Here's the step-by-step approach — assess, prioritize, wrap, modernize, retire — plus how nearshore teams de-risk it.","readMin":6,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/legacy-strategy.webp","imageAlt":"An IT architect reviewing a modernization roadmap, a legacy modernization strategy"},{"title":"Legacy modernization tools (2026)","slug":"legacy-modernization-tools-2026","category":"Insight","excerpt":"The best tools for legacy system modernization in 2026, sorted by job — assessment, code analysis, API wrapping, cloud migration, and AI-assisted translation. What each category does and how to pick.","readMin":7,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/legacy-tools-v2.webp","imageAlt":"A developer using modern tools, legacy modernization tools for 2026"},{"title":"Modernize vs rebuild: which is right for your legacy system?","slug":"modernize-vs-rebuild","category":"Guide","excerpt":"Modernize vs rebuild is the first real decision in any legacy project. Modernizing keeps your working business logic and upgrades it incrementally; rebuilding starts from scratch. Here's how to choose — and why a big-bang rewrite is rarely worth the risk.","readMin":6,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/legacy-modernize-rebuild.webp","imageAlt":"An IT engineer in a data center aisle, modernize vs rebuild a legacy system"},{"title":"What is legacy system modernization? (2026 guide)","slug":"what-is-legacy-system-modernization","category":"Guide","excerpt":"Legacy system modernization is the process of updating outdated software — old code, mainframes, and aging platforms — so it runs on modern infrastructure without losing business logic. Here's what it means, the main approaches, what it costs, and how to do it without breaking the business.","readMin":6,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/legacy-what-is.webp","imageAlt":"An IT engineer working on servers, illustrating what legacy system modernization is"}],"className":"mt-8"}]]}]
